    "suggested_branch": "claude/wp167-analytics-external-history-foundation",
    "objective": "Create the first local, offline, read-only-against-canonical analytical research plane over the merged point-in-time evidence system: deterministic derived Parquet materialization of verified dataset snapshot references with logical-versus-physical identity separation, a provenance-separated external-history descriptor proven with the pmxt v2 representative local adapter (no downloader, no network), and DuckDB/Polars read-only queries with parity. Canonical SQLite records and manifests remain the sole integrity authority; Parquet is derived only. Adds exactly pyarrow==25.0.1, duckdb==1.5.5, polars==1.44.1 and moves the Python floor to >=3.12,<3.15. No NautilusTrader, WebSocket, Data API, Hermes, strategy, paper, credentials, execution, live, or scheduler.",
    "capital_at_risk_usd": 0,
    "xl_explicit_authorization": true,
    "xl_authorization_basis": "Explicit user XL authorization, expanded in two further explicit authorizations to 29 files. WP167 is one coherent capability; the nine files beyond the original 20 are mandatory governance regression guards caused by the authorized implementation (the architecture-boundary approved-source guard, the project-status current-phase guard, and seven historical scope/reconciliation guards that must gain a narrow WP167 branch), each preserving every historical WP's exact-scope assertions. WP166 updated the same class of guards. Exact governed scope is 29 files."
